\details{
\strong{Bubble or menu?} A menu lets the visitor ask the app to do something: attach
it with \verb{click =} and read the choice from \verb{input$<id>_menu}. For a message the
app sends to the visitor, use \code{\link[=mascot_bubble]{mascot_bubble()}} and \code{update_mascot(id, bubble = ...)}.

\strong{Where the menu opens.} The menu must fit in the space where it can show. For
an inline mascot, that space is bounded by the nearest container that scrolls
or clips (such as a \code{bslib::card()} body or a sidebar), not the whole window.
For a floating mascot, it uses the window. When the chosen \code{direction} has no
room there, the menu opens on the opposite side; when neither side has room, it
opens wherever \code{"auto"} finds space. So \code{direction = "bottom"} on a mascot near
the bottom of a card opens above it. Give the mascot room on the chosen side,
or use \code{"auto"}.

\strong{Keyboard navigation.} Enter or Space on the focused mascot opens or closes
the menu and moves the focus to its first item; holding the key down toggles
it once. After opening it with a click, the down and up arrows move from the
mascot to the first or last item. Use the arrow keys, Home and End to move
between items, and press Escape to close the menu and return focus to the
mascot.

\strong{Reading the selection in Shiny.} Choosing an item sets \verb{input$<id>_menu} to
the item ID (for example, \code{input$helper_menu} for \code{mascot("helper")}).
Choosing the same item twice triggers the input twice. Opening and closing the
menu never set \verb{input$<id>_click}; that input is only for \code{\link[=mascot_action]{mascot_action()}}.
